cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below. The formulas for L*_n that it
  implements are proved in arXiv:2610.22622 and arXiv:2610.28504; please cite those
  papers for the mathematics.
title: Square Packing
version: 0.2.0
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Badger
    given-names: Matthew
    affiliation: University of Connecticut
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/matthew-badger/square-packing-game"
url: "https://tangentmeasure.com/square-packing-game/"
abstract: >-
  A browser game on packing 4 to 8 axis-parallel squares into the smallest square
  frame, with 29 levels (one for each optimal packing strategy up to eight squares) and
  a free-play mode. The frame side L*_n and every hint and answer are computed from the
  exact closed formulas for L*_n, n <= 8, and their canonical packings.
keywords:
  - square packing
  - translative packing
  - axis-parallel squares
  - discrete geometry
  - mathematical game
